PAGES = [
{"index": 228, "printed_page": "420", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "420"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "27. Dignity of labour."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "28. Classless society."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "29. How can we build a strong nation?"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "30. Importance of character."},
{"type": "heading", "text": "Some Hints For Speech Test"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Suppose three subjects below are given. How could you go about it?"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Games and sports."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Ideal of a military officer."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Why do you want to join the services?"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Were you to choose the first subject, you would quickly make a mental note of the points that come uppermost in your reckoning."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Games provide relaxation. The body gets as much attention as the mind. Discipline, team spirit, leadership, co-operation, sportsmanship, initiative, toughness, mind and body remain equally strong......"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "In the second subject, ideal of a military officer, like points could be gathered beginning with sound education, love of country, discipline, character, daring, initiative, spirit of adventure, impartiality and sympathy, punctuality, social popularity, neatness and smart appearance......"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The third subject will call for points, which the individual one can decide. Among other things, love for country and a desire to defend her, discipline and valuable training, stipend during training, steady career, healthy life, adventure......"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The mind should be so trained as to yield points at short notice. Once the train of thoughts starts, the flow will be easy. During the ten days, several speeches should be prepared in advance. No attempt at memorizing, however, should be made, trusting the mind to cope with the situation."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Advice to the Candidates:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. Select the subject on which you can get the greatest number of points within the limited time at your disposal."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. Arrange your thoughts before you begin to speak. Then stand in an easy position to speak to the group. Avoid resting on one leg and the other alternately. Then start with these words: \"Mr. GTO and Friends, I am going to express a few thoughts on ...... (mention the subject)."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. Avoid unnecessary movements of hands and legs as these show nervousness."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. Speak in a moderately high and pleasant voice so that everybody could hear you and enjoy your lecture."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "5. Be careful to avoid politics and controversial points. Men in the armed forces are expected to be above politics and other matters that divide people and cause conflicts. Keeping these things in mind, you have to speak accordingly."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "6. As far as possible, follow the order that is natural so as to impress upon the GTO that you can present your ideas clearly."},
]},
{"index": 229, "printed_page": "421", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "Dogar's Unique up-to-date ISSB GUIDE"},
{"type": "header", "text": "421"},
{"type": "title", "text": "OLQ"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(Officers Like Qualities)"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Important and essential qualities of a service officer (which ISSB look for in the prospective candidates), are given as under. The candidates are advised to inculcate and cultivate these \"OLQ (officers like qualities) Factors\"."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(a) Factor I—Planning and Organisation:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) Effective Intelligence: Capability to deal with practical situation and act as per recruitment of the situation."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) Reasoning Ability: Ability to grasp and uptake the situation and arrive at conclusion, by rational thinking."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) Organising Ability: Ability to plan and organize resources (and to make their best use) capacity to finish the given task in a systematic manner (within the stipulated period)."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) Power of Expression: Ability to put across one's point/idea clearly and vividly with ease. One should be a good orator and also a good listener. Candidate should speak fluently with confidence."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(b) Factor II—Social Adjustment:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) Social Adoptability: To adopt to changing environment and also to adjust accordingly."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) Co-operation: Participation in working together. Harmony and helping each other."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) Sense of Responsibility: Willing to discharge responsibility and given duty."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(c) Factor III—Social Effectiveness:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) Initiative: Ability to initiate (start) and sustain act."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) Self-Confidence: Faith in one's ability to meet critical situation and event."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) Speed of Decision: Capability to arrive at workable situation judiciously and expeditiously."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) Ability to Influence Group: Ability to bring about willing effect from the group."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(v) Liveliness (Cheerfulness): Capacity to keep one buoyant."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(vi) Resourcefulness: Capability of the leader to deal with the situation without normal available means and material."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(d) Factor IV—Dynamicism:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) Determination: A firm resolution. It implies fixedness of purpose, concentration and will-power."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) Courage: Ability to take bold preposed risks."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) Stamina: Capacity to withstand physical and mental stress and strain to undergo prolonged endurance."},
]},
{"index": 230, "printed_page": "", "blocks": [
{"type": "title", "text": "GENERAL INSTRUCTIONS/ ADVICE TO CANDIDATES"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. Candidate must remain cool, calm and collective. He should be normal and natural during the period of selection."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. He should not look serious (like aghast). He should take everything casually."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. He should be helpful and cooperative with other candidates. He must not show selfishness or remain aloof. He should behave like a perfect gentleman."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. He should look smart and properly dressed; especially when appearing before interviewing officer."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "5. He must remain alert and listen to given instructions carefully and work intelligently."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "6. It should be noted that the aim of ISSB members is to assess and discover candidate's innate and inner personality. He should have all-round and well-balanced harmonious development."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "7. The members of ISSB are not there to reject you outright, but on the contrary, they probe into your wholesome personality. They discover in you, \"Officer Like Qualities\"."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "8. A defence officer has to act and react as per the gravity of situation. He must take accurate and correct decision in the fitness of things."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "9. It is of paramount importance that a candidate cooperates fully with all the members of the Board. Yours' this aspect will enable them to find your traits and characteristics."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "10. Do not try to bluff. If you do not know the correct answer of any question; say \"sorry\" and regret for your ignorance. A candidate must be sincere, reliable and straight forward. He should not feel disgusted or defeated for having been 'Not-Selected'. There may be many other avenues open for you or else be a computer engineer, scientist, or a philosopher."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "****************"},
]},
{"index": 231, "printed_page": "", "blocks": [
{"type": "title", "text": "Group Planning (Military Planning)"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Introduction:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "This is an indoor test, employed by GTO, with a view to test the planning ability of the candidate. It deals with certain difficult problems, described in various situations. GTO tests a candidate's mental alertness, grasping power, power of understanding and finally finding out correct solution within the stipulated time. Here in the group task, a candidate's capacity to work in team or group is also adjudged."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "GTO issues a copy of the printed narrative to each candidate. Thereafter, he explains the various details and situations existed therein. It is explained on 'Sand Model' and GTO ensures that each candidate has fully understood the problem and situations. The (candidates are hence advised to read the narrative fully) GTO asked candidates again to have their doubts cleared."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Once candidates have understood the narrative, GTO directed them to write their solution on a sheet of paper. After the written work is over, candidates (as a group) are asked to discuss the given situation and problem at length. They are supposed to arrive at a solution, acceptable to all members. Once the final plan is accepted, one of the candidates is asked to read the Final Plan. (This plan is only made after heated discussion on the situation and problem given by GTO)."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "General Instructions (To Candidates):"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. Candidates must read carefully, the instruction given by GTO and jot-down its minutest detail."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. Ensure that you have fully and correctly understood the requirements of problem. In case of doubts, these points can be clarified."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. It is of paramount importance that you take active part in group planning and discussion. Give your thoughtful solution with confidence and clarity."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. Don't interrupt anyone, who is speaking or giving a solution. You should only speak when someone's points/ideas you are likely to put forth."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "5. It is utmost necessary to remember for Military Planning:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "(1) Time at your disposal (2) Men with you (3) Material and equipment with you."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "****************"},
]},
{"index": 232, "printed_page": "424", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "424"},
{"type": "header", "text": "GTO's Tasks"},
{"type": "title", "text": "EXERCISES"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "There are given some exercises to come up \"Group Planning\"."},
{"type": "heading", "text": "EXERCISE I"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Narrative:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "You are leading a party of 10 men. They are provided with arms, ammunition and a jeep. You are confronted with the following situations:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. You have been allotted one hour of time. Within this period, you have been alerted that there is likelihood of a sabotage on the railway line 2 km from Railway Station."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. Again you noticed that an Air Crash has taken place in hillocks 5 km from Railway Station."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. You also learnt that terrorists had struck in village Alipur 15 km away."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. One villager came running to you to inform you that a tigress has mauled 2 women and they are lying unconscious in the forest nearby."},
{"type": "image", "text": "Sketch map showing Hospital, Rly. Stn., Train, Village Alipur, Mosque, Place of Sabotage, Site of Air Crash, Forest and Hillocks"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Aim:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(a) To stop train at least one km away from the place of sabotage (to avoid colossal loss of lives)."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(b) To render all possible assistance to victims of air crash. Arrange their safety, movements to nearby hospitals and encircle the area to prevent bad elements from nefarious design."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(c) To apprehend or kill the terrorist that struck in the village."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(d) To give first aid to injured in the forest and remove them to nearby hospital."},
]},
{"index": 233, "printed_page": "425", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "Dogar's Unique up-to-date ISSB GUIDE"},
{"type": "header", "text": "425"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Suggested Plan:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. As party commander, I will inform the civil authorities immediately (a) Both station masters of incoming/outcoming railway stations (b) Civil Police authorities (c) Civil Hospital authorities (d) Villagers (especially Ex-Servicemen there)."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. I will send one man together with a jeep and driver to stop the train. This man will be instructed to give signal to driver of train to stop it (by any red cloth, or red flag, or any red article). He will explain to the driver about the 'Sabotage', who will take necessary action."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. With the help of police and medical authorities, we will cordon off the area of air crash: Render all possible assistance to victims and shift them to place of safety. Dead/injured will be removed to nearby hospital."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. A force of local youngmen (especially Ex-servicemen with arms) will be mobilized and encircle the village to face the terrorists and eliminate them from scene."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "5. Send one man with gun for injured ladies in forest."},
{"type": "heading", "text": "EXERCISE II"},
{"type": "heading", "text": "HIDDEN TREASURE"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Narrative:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "You are company commander. 6 men are detailed for the task. You have got a rowing boat, rope, and a mechanical boat."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Commander asked you to locate hidden treasure dumped by the robbers in hillock across the lake. Treasure is always guarded by 2 men round-the-clock. How to get back treasure?"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Suggested Plan:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. I will watch the activities of the robbers."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. Approach to hillock where treasure is hidden by boats."},
{"type": "image", "text": "Sketch showing hillocks with treasure in cave, lake, rowing boat, mechanical boat and camp"},
]},
{"index": 234, "printed_page": "426", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "426"},
{"type": "header", "text": "GTO's Tasks"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Task:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. If our men will go by boat during daytime to destination (cave where treasure is hidden), they will be observed and attacked."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. During a night, rowing boat cannot function smoothly and will make noise while rowing."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. I along with my 2 active men (who are expert) will move by mechanical boat. Other jawans will be alerted on our reaching. We will switch off the machinery of boat (when it has attained momentum) and take the enemy by surprise, supported by our remaining soldiers who follow us at a distance in rowing boat and are well-equipped. Then robbers will be nabbed during night and booty will be recovered. Robbers will be handed over to police and treasure handed over to Government."},
{"type": "heading", "text": "EXERCISE III"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "You are commander of men, material and time as given below:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. 8 Armedmen"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. Time—4 p.m. to 6 p.m."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. Jeep"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. Boating facilities"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Task:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. You are asked to protect the golden idol being smuggled from Temple (A) by foreigner and being flown away from Air Strip (B)."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. You are to safeguard govt. treasure which is being looted by robbers at Railway Station nearby a Village (C)."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. Protect your men and material from any loss."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. Protect any sabotage activity."},
{"type": "image", "text": "Sketch map showing Temple A with golden idol, boat, ferry, aerostrip runway B, P. Stn., villages, hillock, dispensary, road, Rly line, signals, Rly Stn, Treasure Govt., village C"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Students are advised to make necessary plan to achieve the said objective."},
]},
{"index": 235, "printed_page": "", "blocks": [
{"type": "title", "text": "Group Tasks : Outdoor Tests"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Introduction:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "If nature is against us, we shall fight Nature and make it obey."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "—Simon Bolivar"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Thus from the war of Nature, from famine and death, the most excited objects which we are capable of conceiving, namely, the production of the higher animals, directly follows."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "—Charles Darwin, The Origin of the Species"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "\"The Right of Nature\", which writers commonly call jus naturale, is the liberty each man hath, to use his own power, as he will himself, for the preservation of his own nature, that is to save his own life; and consequently, of doing anything, which in his own judgement and reason he shall conceive to be the aptest means thereunto."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "—Thomas Hobbes, Leviathan, Part 2, of Commonwealth"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The objective of the Indoor Tests and the Outdoor Tests is one and the same, which is to assess the suitability of a candidate for training as an officer in the Defence Services. The purpose is to discover the potential leaders of fighters in the defence of the country."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The Outdoor Tests have a great potentiality of discovering the true qualities of a candidate for his fitness in the Defence Services, because the Armed Forces essentially lead an outdoor life and they are perpetually under outdoor tests all their professional careers."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The outdoor tests are directed to discover qualities of leadership, intellect, initiative, originality of ideas, planning and organisation, self-confidence and spirit of cooperation."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Kinds of Outdoor Group Tests:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The GTO orders the following tests in the following order:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) Progressive Group Task"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) Inter Group Obstacle Race or Snake Race"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) Half-Group Task"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) Individual Obstacles"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(v) Command Task"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(vi) Final Group Task"},
{"type": "heading", "text": "PHYSICAL TASKS"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "For these physical tasks candidate should be carrying white short shirt, while shorts, white canvas shoes and white socks."},
{"type": "heading", "text": "1. PROGRESSIVE GROUP TASK"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "This task falls in outdoor series of tasks. In this task a group of 8 to 0 candidates are required to cross 4 obstacles of hindrances or restrictions in 40 minutes as a whole group. In tackling these hindrances, the candidates have to attach much importance to"},
]},
{"index": 236, "printed_page": "428", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "428"},
{"type": "header", "text": "GTO's Tasks"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "bridge, lever and swing as well as the helping material which they have to carry while crossing obstacles. Group testing officer will explain the nature and rules of task in the beginning."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Helpful Hints for Progressive Group task"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "In tackling the obstacles of \"Progressive Group Task\", there are as a matter of fact, three main principles which are involved. They are, lever, bridge and swing. The plank or planks that are employed as helping material can be used either in the form of a lever or bridge according to the circumstances. A rope should invariably be tied, as the case may be, to the remotest end of the lever or bridge. This is very essential because it becomes impossible for the candidates to get or pull back the plank once they crossed over.Some of the fundamental rules which the Group Testing Officer clears to the candidates before beginning the task are;"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. Out of Bounds Rule"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The whole ground area and any other structure painted red between the start line and the finish line, and their helping materials and loads are out of bounds to the candidates. There is punishment for any candidate or any object that touches the out of bounds. The defaulter have soon to go back to the star line of that obstacle. If any object touches the out bounds areas, then the object should be carried back by the defaulter to the stat-line and then it should be brought forward again."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. The Four Feet Rule"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The candidates are not permitted to jump any distance exceeding 4 feet either in length or in height. Such distances, are to be crossed with the assistance of the helping materials (ropes or bellies)."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. The Group Rule"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Every obstacle should be crossed by the whole group with its material and load, before the next obstacle is tried by anybody in the group."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. The Time Rule"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The task should be concluded in 40 minutes. There is no time limit for each of the four obstacles which are included in this task."},
{"type": "image", "text": "Diagram titled Progressive Group Task showing Starting Line, Finish Line, fixed and moveable drums (T, R, Q, S, P), plank and ropes"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Example 1.1: In the following hindrances, with the assistance of a plank and two ropes, the candidates are required to cross it over, where candidates are forbidden to jump up or down or cover a distance of four feet. There is punishment for any candidate or any object that touches the out of bounds red area. The time require to tackle the hindrances is"},
]},
{"index": 237, "printed_page": "", "blocks": [
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "40 minutes."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Objectives:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The main objectives of the test are—"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) to test candidates' ability to tackle problems of practical nature which one may find in life;"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) to test the practical ability of the candidates to work in a team;"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) to find out the planning ability of the candidate;"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) to find out the resourceful of the candidates i.e., the ability to utilize manpower and material; and"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(v) to find the candidates' attitude towards the other members of the team."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Nature of Group Obstacles:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "These obstacle exercises are leaderless group exercises, which cannot be tackled by a single individual alone. The entire group is required to work in a spirit of cooperation. However, the candidates must remember that these exercises admit of a number of solutions and candidates of average intelligence can do these exercises if they think with a cool head. They should not become nervous at the very sight of the obstacle."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "General PGT Requirements:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. The candidates have to cross some obstacles from the SL (Start Line) to FL (Finish Line), both of which are clearly marked out."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. The candidates have to carry a certain load of a burden or a burden of a load on a stretcher."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. They also carry supplementary materials, like ballis, ropes and planks, from SL to FL."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. Certain areas are marked \"Out of Bounds\" which have to be avoided."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "5. Certain material or structures marked \"red\" between SL and FL must not be touched."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Procedure:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The following procedure is adopted for the administration of this test:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. The GTO explains the needs of the test to the candidates that they have to carry a certain load with the supporting material from the Start Line (SL) to the Finish Line (FL)."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. He explains what is \"Out of Bounds\" and what materials and structures are not to be touched. \"Out of bounds\" means places where the candidates are not allowed to go."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. The GTO gives the candidates the supporting materials which have to be carried along throughout and which are essential for the solution of problems."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. They are also told about other rules which must be borne in mind."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "5. All obstacles are explained and clarified to the candidates one after the other."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "6. Then GTO asks the candidates to understand everything and have their doubts clarified before they proceed to the solution of obstacles."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Rules and Penalties:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. If any candidate touches any point in the area marked \"Out of Bounds\", he has to bear the penalty by going back with material to the Start Line of that particular obstacle and begin anew."},
]},
{"index": 238, "printed_page": "", "blocks": [
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. The entire group must cross the obstacle before they are allowed to tackle the next obstacle."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. The candidates are permitted to jump distances up to one metre in length and height. Distances beyond one metre have to be crossed with the help of supporting material like ballis, planks or ropes."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. All obstacles have to be crossed and completed by all in forty minutes."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "5. The path to be followed must be strictly adhered to."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Simple Engineering Principles:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The candidates are allowed to follow simple engineering principles in overcoming their obstacles:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) They can make a lever by combination of planks with rope tied at one end and supported by a drum."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) The two ends of a plank supported on two drums serve the purpose of a bridge."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) You can tie one end of a rope to a pole or branch of a tree and swing with the other end."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) Ropes can be used to serve as a ladder."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Advice to Candidates:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. Listen carefully when GTO is explaining rules and follow them to avoid pitfalls."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. Keep in view the various supporting materials available and employ them effectively for the removal of obstacles."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. Keep all members in view and use their contribution in full cooperation for solution of problems."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. All members should discuss together and work together for the tackling of solutions."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "5. Men and materials should be organized to overcome an obstacle quickly and smoothly. Opinions of all members should be considered by all."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "6. Help the leader actively at every step in the speedy execution of the project."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "7. Make your best contribution at all times in a team spirit."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "8. Show your promptitude, initiative, dash and drive in the overcoming of obstacles."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "9. Be ready to take reasonable risk in the common cause."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "10. Do not waste time in indecisiveness. Be active and do everything possible in cooperation with others."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "11. If you touch anything marked red or out of bounds, do not hide the fact from GTO but be ready to pay the penalty."},
{"type": "heading", "text": "ILLUSTRATION"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "I. Obstacle Number One"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(A) Given men and material"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) A group of eight/ten candidates."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) A wooden plank six feet long."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) Two ropes each about 16 feet in length."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) A casualty tied on a stretcher, generally a sand bag or ammunition box."},
]},
{"index": 239, "printed_page": "431", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "Dogar's Unique up-to-date ISSB GUIDE"},
{"type": "header", "text": "431"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(B) Structures"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "As shown in the following sketch:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) Four fixed drums D1, D2, D3, D4 of one foot diameter each."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) Two hanging ropes R1 and R2."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) A tyre T hanging with a rope and capable of swinging in all directions."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) Three bench-like structures B1, B2, B3 are fixed in the ground and can accommodate 3 to 4 persons on the top. These are about 2½ feet high."},
{"type": "image", "text": "Sketch of obstacle course with start lines (S) and finish lines (F), drums D1-D4, ropes R1, R2, tyre T, benches B1-B3, plank, stretcher and ropes"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(C) Requirement"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "All men and material must get on the other side (beyond the finish line) in the minimum time but not more than twenty minutes."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "N.B."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) S.L. stands for start line and F.L. for finish line."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) Ground between the start line (S.L.) and the finish line (F.L.) is out of bounds."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) Portion marked red in any structure is 'out of bounds'."},
]},
{"index": 240, "printed_page": "430", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "430"},
{"type": "header", "text": "GTO's Tasks"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. The entire group must cross the obstacle before they are allowed to tackle the next obstacle."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. The candidates are permitted to jump distances up to one metre in length and height. Distances beyond one metre have to be crossed with the help of supporting material like ballis, planks or ropes."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. All obstacles have to be crossed and completed by all in forty minutes."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "5. The path to be followed must be strictly adhered to."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Simple Engineering Principles:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The candidates are allowed to follow simple engineering principles in overcoming their obstacles:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) They can make a lever by combination of planks with rope tied at one end and supported by a drum."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) The two ends of a plank supported on two drums serve the purpose of a bridge."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) You can tie one end of a rope to a pole or branch of a tree and swing with the other end."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) Ropes can be used to serve as a ladder."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Advice to Candidates:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "1. Listen carefully when GTO is explaining rules and follow them to avoid pitfalls."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "2. Keep in view the various supporting materials available and employ them effectively for the removal of obstacles."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "3. Keep all members in view and use their contribution in full cooperation for solution of problems."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "4. All members should discuss together and work together for the tackling of solutions."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "5. Men and materials should be organized to overcome an obstacle quickly and smoothly. Opinions of all members should be considered by all."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "6. Help the leader actively at every step in the speedy execution of the project."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "7. Make your best contribution at all times in a team spirit."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "8. Show your promptitude, initiative, dash and drive in the overcoming of obstacles."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "9. Be ready to take reasonable risk in the common cause."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "10. Do not waste time in indecisiveness. Be active and do everything possible in cooperation with others."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "11. If you touch anything marked red or out of bounds, do not hide the fact from GTO but be ready to pay the penalty."},
{"type": "heading", "text": "ILLUSTRATION"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "I. Obstacle Number One"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(A) Given men and material"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) A group of eight/ten candidates."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) A wooden plank six feet long."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) Two ropes each about 16 feet in length."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) A casualty tied on a stretcher, generally a sand bag or ammunition box."},
]},
{"index": 241, "printed_page": "431", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "Dogar's Unique up-to-date ISSB GUIDE"},
{"type": "header", "text": "431"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(B) Structures"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "As shown in the following sketch:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) Four fixed drums D1, D2, D3, D4 of one foot diameter each."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) Two hanging ropes R1 and R2."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) A tyre T hanging with a rope and capable of swinging in all directions."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) Three bench-like structures B1, B2, B3 are fixed in the ground and can accommodate 3 to 4 persons on the top. These are about 2½ feet high."},
{"type": "image", "text": "Sketch of obstacle course with start lines (S) and finish lines (F), drums D1-D4, ropes R1, R2, tyre T, benches B1-B3, plank, stretcher and ropes"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(C) Requirement"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "All men and material must get on the other side (beyond the finish line) in the minimum time but not more than twenty minutes."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "N.B."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) S.L. stands for start line and F.L. for finish line."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) Ground between the start line (S.L.) and the finish line (F.L.) is out of bounds."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) Portion marked red in any structure is 'out of bounds'."},
]},
{"index": 242, "printed_page": "432", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "432"},
{"type": "header", "text": "GTO's Tasks"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(D) Hints for Solution"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(a) Bridge the gap between D2 and B2 with plank and pass on men and materials to position B2."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(b) Make use of the hanging tyre to rest on side of stretcher while tying up the ropes to the other."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(c) Pull the rope R2 by throwing the spare rope around it. Rope R1 is not used. Let the persons swing to drum D4. Casualty on stretcher can also be swung across holding the ropes tied to one side."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) Bridge the gap between D4 and Finish Line by means of the plank and go across in shifts."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "II. Obstacle Number Two"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(A) Given men and materials"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Same as in the case of Obstacle No. 1."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(B) Structures"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "As per sketch, Symbols indicate the materials as in the case of Obstacle No. 1 (See Fig. On Page ____)."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(C) Requirements"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "As in Obstacle No. 1."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(v) Hints for Solution"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(a) Bridge in to B1 from D1 with the help of the plank. Then pass over the whole lot to B2."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(b) Two persons to swing across the stumps and then go over to the finish line."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(c) These persons support the plank on their hands and bridge up the gap between B2 and FL."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(d) Now two more persons go over FL and help passing over the casualty."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(e) After the last man goes over the FL, the plank is pulled over with the help of rope tied on to the end resting on B2."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "III. Obstacle Number Three"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(A) Given men and materials"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Same as in Obstacle No. 1."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(B) Structures"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "In addition to the symbols given in Obstacle No. 1, Sindicates wooden stamps of 9\" diameter (See Fig. on page ____)."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(C) Requirements"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Same as in Obstacle No. 1, but time is generally 30 minutes. Try from the center in the following manner:"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(D) Hints for Solution"},
]},
{"index": 243, "printed_page": "", "blocks": [
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(a) Come to B2 by bridging the gap between D1, B1, B1, B2."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(b) Make another bridge by tying rope to one end of the plank and put it on to D2."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(c) Finally jump over beyond the FL."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(d) The casualty to be supported by men already on FL and 2 men on the other side."},
{"type": "heading", "text": "II. INTER-GROUP OBSTACLE-RACE"},
{"type": "heading", "text": "(OR SNAKE RACE)"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Inter-Group Obstacle Race is sometimes called the Snake Race by the Boards. In this, there are four sets of similar obstacles running parallel to one another, which all the four groups have to negotiate in competition."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Objectives:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "This race is intended to find out"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(i) physical fitness;"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(ii) courage and determination;"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iii) co-operation;"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(iv) team spirit; and"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(v) attitude to each other in a leaderless group."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Advice to the candidates:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(1) While negotiating your obstacles, remember that the achievement of the team is to be judged and therefore you must help the weaker members of the team."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(2) Take on yourself the maximum responsibility and exertion that you can possibly take."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(3) Do not hesitate or waver in taking any risk."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(4) Show specific dash and determination in tackling these obstacles."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(5) Do no try to show off. Your contribution will be automatically noticed by the GTO."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(6) Do not show any lack of diffidence even if you cannot come out first."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Rules:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The rules to be observed in this race and the penalty for non-observance of the rules are the same as for the Progressive Group Task."},
{"type": "heading", "text": "ILLUSTRATION"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Obstacle Number One:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Given men and materials: (i) A group of eight candidates; (ii) A casualty tied on a stretcher. Generally, it is a bomboo around which a tent is tied."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Structures: The three vertical structures as shown in the figure on page."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Requirement: To cross over the obstacle as a group."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Suggestions: Two candidates cross over to the other side, and another two set on the middle structure to help in passing over the casualty. Finally, all the remaining"},
]},
{"index": 244, "printed_page": "434", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "434"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "persons pass over individually."},
{"type": "caption", "text": "INTER-GROUP OBSTACLE RACE"},
{"type": "image", "text": "Diagram of four parallel obstacles (1 to 4) with start (S) and finish (F) lines: ladder with casualty, horizontal balli fixtures, plank bridge with ropes, plastered wall with net, slanting ballis structure"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Obstacle Number Two:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Given men and materials: Same as in the case of Obstacle No. 1."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Structures: Two longish balli fixtures connected by a bridge consisting of a plank swinging on both sides by double ropes."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Requirement: As in the case of Obstacle No.1"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Suggestions: Sit on the balli and then slide along. Two persons to pass over to the other end. Two persons to sit on the plank and assist in passing on the stretcher to the people on the farther balli. Rest of the party may be helped to cross over."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Obstacle Number Three:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Given men and material: The same as in obstacle."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Structures: A cemented and plastered wall of 8 feet in height. A net of thin ropes tied on the top which can support the weight of 4 men."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Requirement: Same as in obstacle."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Suggestions: Two men cross over the wall and jump to the other side. Two men sit on the top and assist in passing the casualty. Remaining men cross on their own."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Obstacle Number Four:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Given men and materials: The same as in the case of Obstacle No.1"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Structure: It consists of a horizontal balli supported by slanting ballis."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Requirement: As in the case of Obstacle No.1"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Suggestions: Two persons to cross the obstacle first. Two to stay on the top balli take over the stretcher from rear and pass to those who have already crossed. The remaining persons cross individually."},
]},
{"index": 245, "printed_page": "", "blocks": [
{"type": "heading", "text": "2. HALF GROUP TASK"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "In Half Group Task candidates of a group who are, usually 8 to 10 are divided into two groups. In this task, each half group has to face only a single hindrance. They must carry the main material and the helping material with them, on crossing the obstacle to the other side of the obstacle. Example (1.2)"},
{"type": "image", "text": "Diagram titled Half Group Task showing Finishing Line, Starting Line, wooden platforms R and Q, moveable drum P, and three small planks"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Within the starting line and the finishing line, there are two wooden platform Q and R and a moveable drum P. The middle portion of the drum which is marked red, is out of bounds. There are also three small planks lying outside the starting line. The candidate should cross over from the starting line to the finishing line with the aid of those small planks."},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "This task is so arranged as to confront the half group with a fairly difficult task. Here the group is divided into two halves and each group is put on the test separately. The purpose is to see a fewer boys working in a small group, where in all of them can put their hands to the work and can contribute something in a leaderless group. It must, however, be remembered that it is essentially a group task and the members must work for the group in spirit of cooperation and coordination."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Obstacles:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "In this task, there is usually one obstacle to be tackled and time allowed is 10 to 15 minutes. The rules governing this task and the principles remembered while tackling it are the same as for other group tasks, and therefore these are not repeated here in detail."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "The Requirement:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Remember that the candidates have to carry a load like a drum from the start line to the finish line and they are given helping material like ballis, rope and plank."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "The Rules:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The rules to be followed are that the entire area between the start and the finish line as also any material painted red is out of bounds for the candidates as well as to their load or helping material. Again, candidates are allowed to jump distances up to a maximum of 4 feet in length or height. Distances beyond 4 feet have to be crossed with the help of helping material like ballis, plank or rope."},
]},
{"index": 246, "printed_page": "436", "blocks": [
{"type": "header", "text": "436"},
{"type": "header", "text": "GTO's Tasks"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "The Devices:"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "The devices to be used are:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(a) combination of plank with rope tie at one end and propped on a drum, thus making a lever;"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(b) plank supported on two drums, thus making a bridge; and"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(c) tying one end of a rope to a pole and swing with the other end."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(d) using the rope as a ladder."},
{"type": "caption", "text": "HALF-GROUP TASK (HGT)"},
{"type": "image", "text": "Diagram of Half-Group Task: drum, rope, plank and four men at start; S.L, F.L; drum D1, bench-like structure B, drum D2"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "Method to be followed:"},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(a) The GTO tells the candidates the requirement of the test."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(b) He tells them what material like the balli and the rope will help the candidates in tackling of the problem."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(c) Further, he will explain the rules to be followed by them."},
{"type": "numbered", "text": "(d) After this, he asks the candidates to have their doubts removed. When he is sure, that they have all followed the rules and instructions, he asks them to set about the task."},
{"type": "heading", "text": "ILLUSTRATION"},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(A) Given men and material"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "4 persons, an empty drum, a rope, a plank about 6 feet long."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(B) Structures"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "As shown in the sketch, on page 253, there are two fixed drums on either side of the fixture which is a bench-like structure in the middle, which is 6 feet high, D1, and D2. (See Fig. above). Two persons can easily stay on the top plank of this structure."},
{"type": "subheading", "text": "(C) Requirement"},
{"type": "paragraph", "text": "To cross over the obstacles with men and material from the start line (SL) to the finishing line (FL)."},
]},
]
